``dials.integrate``: The memory estimate used to limit the number of processes, and to decide whether to split the reflection table, has been made more accurate. Shoebox pixels are now counted for the time they are actually allocated, rather than at 12 bytes per pixel for the whole lifetime of each shoebox. The estimate now also includes costs that were previously missing: the Shoebox objects themselves, the frame lookup, the columns added to the reflection table during integration, and the cached image and mask (13 bytes per detector pixel). The new memory report line "Memory required for images" shows the image part. Integration also no longer builds an unused graph of overlapping reflections for each job, which saves memory on datasets with many overlaps.
